# What NOT to upload to the EAS build server.
#
# Without this the archive was 1.1 GB and took 3m38s to upload, because the
# whole source corpus went with it — raw CTET booklets, NCERT textbook PDFs,
# parsed JSON. None of it is used by the Android build: the app reads exactly
# one content file, assets/content/studymate.db, which the export produces and
# which IS uploaded.
#
# .easignore replaces .gitignore for build uploads rather than adding to it, so
# anything that must stay excluded has to be repeated here.

# ── the corpus (hundreds of MB of source PDFs) ────────────────────────────────
../../content/
../../dist/
../../tools/
../../apps/api/

# ── build output and caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
android/
ios/
.expo/
node_modules/
dist/
web-build/

# ── local noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.tmp
.DS_Store
coverage/
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── secrets, in case one is ever written here ─────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
*.keystore
*.jks
